      "text": "To find the product of the greatest common divisor (GCD) and the least common multiple (LCM) of \\(18\\) and \\(42\\), we can use the relationship between the GCD and LCM of two numbers, which is given by:\n\n\\[\n\\text{GCD}(a, b) \\times \\text{LCM}(a, b) = a \\times b\n\\]\n\nHere, \\(a = 18\\) and \\(b = 42\\). First, we need to find the GCD of \\(18\\) and \\(42\\).\n\n### Step 1: Find the prime factorizations\n- The prime factorization of \\(18\\) is:\n  \\[\n  18 = 2 \\times 3^2\n  \\]\n- The prime factorization of \\(42\\) is:\n  \\[\n  42 = 2 \\times 3 \\times 7\n  \\]\n\n### Step 2: Identify the common and unique prime factors\n- The common prime factors are \\(2\\) and \\(3\\).\n- The unique prime factors for \\(18\\) are \\(2\\) and \\(3\\).\n- The unique prime factors for \\(42\\) are \\(2\\), \\(3\\), and \\(7\\).\n\n### Step 3: Determine the GCD\n- The GCD is found by taking the lowest power of each common prime factor:\n  \\[\n  \\text{GCD}(18, 42) = 2^1 \\times 3^1 = 6\n  \\]\n\n### Step 4: Determine the LCM\n- The LCM is found by taking the highest power of each prime factor present in either number:\n  \\[\n  \\text{LCM}(18, 42) = 2^1 \\times 3^2 \\times 7^1 = 2 \\times 9 \\times 7 = 126\n  \\]\n\n### Step 5: Calculate the product of the GCD and the LCM\n\\[\n\\text{GCD}(18, 42) \\times \\text{LCM}(18, 42) = 6 \\times 126\n\\]\n\n### Step 6: Perform the multiplication\n\\[\n6 \\times 126 = 756\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of the greatest common divisor and the least common multiple of \\(18\\) and \\(42\\) is \\(\\boxed{756}\\).",
